{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And you shall give it for the service of the Tent of Meeting.</b> This teaches that they were commanded to count them at the start of the donation for the Tabernacle, after the deed of the calf, because a plague had struck them — as it says, ״וַיִּגֹּף ה׳ אֶת הָעָם״. A parable: to a flock beloved by its owner, into which a plague fell, and once it passed he said to the shepherd: Please count my sheep and know how many remain in them — to make known that it is beloved by him. And it is impossible to say that this counting is the one spoken of in חֻמַּשׁ הַפְּקוּדִים, for it says of it ״בְּאֶחָד לַחֹדֶשׁ הַשֵּׁנִי״, and the Tabernacle was erected on the first of the first month, as it says ״בְּיוֹם הַחֹדֶשׁ הָרִאשׁוֹן בְּאֶחָד לַחֹדֶשׁ תָּקִים״ וגו' (Exodus 40), and from this counting the sockets were made — from its shekels — as it says ״וַיְהִי מְאַת כִּכַּר הַכֶּסֶף לָצֶקֶת״ וגו' (ibid. 38) — this you have learned: there were two, one at the start of their donation after Yom HaKippurim in the first year, and one in the second year in Iyyar, when the Tabernacle was erected. And if you say: is it possible that in both of them Israel were equal — 600,000 and 3,000 and 550 — for so is stated regarding the silver of those counted of the congregation, and in חֻמַּשׁ הַפְּקוּדִים too it says ״וַיִּהְיוּ כָּל הַפְּקוּדִים שֵׁשׁ מֵאוֹת אֶלֶף וּשְׁלֹשֶׁת אֲלָפִים וַחֲמֵשׁ מֵאוֹת וַחֲמִשִּׁים״ (Numbers 1) — and were they not two years apart, so it is impossible that those who were not twenty years old at the time of the first counting were not counted, and in the second they became twenty! Answer to the matter: with respect to the years of the men they were counted in one year, but for the reckoning of the exodus from Egypt they were two years, because for the exodus from Egypt we count from Nisan, as we learned in tractate Rosh HaShanah (2a), and the Tabernacle was built in the first year and erected in the second, for a new year began on the first of Nisan, but the years of the men are reckoned by the count of the years of the world, which begin from Tishrei. It turns out that both countings were in one year — the first counting was in Tishrei after Yom HaKippurim, when the Omnipresent was reconciled to Israel to forgive them, and they were commanded concerning the Tabernacle, and the second on the first of Iyyar." "<b>For the service of the Tent of Meeting.</b> These are the sockets that were made from it."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "Rashi quotes Exodus 32:35 with the divine name יהוה; rendered here as YHWH per divine-name rules."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:54.989319402Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}